Recently, I used Copilot for a couple of development and troubleshooting tasks that resulted in measurable time savings.

• Rundeck Automation Scripts

Used the latest .NET 10 feature to run standalone C# files directly without creating a full project, instead of using PowerShell scripts.

Used Copilot to generate the initial C# scripts for a Rundeck job that downloads DealCloud site backup files.

Estimated time saved: ~3–4 hours, since I only needed to review and customize the generated code instead of building everything from scratch.



• Azure Pipeline Troubleshooting

Used Copilot to troubleshoot an Azure Pipeline issue related to variable syntax in pipeline conditions.

Identified that runtime expression syntax was required for the condition to work correctly.

Estimated time saved: ~4 hours, as it helped quickly pinpoint the root cause of the issue.

